  "worked_solution": "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OC} & =c=2i+4j-3k, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{OD} & =d=-i+5k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{DC}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DC} & =\\overset{\\to }{OC}-\\overset{\\to }{OD} \\\\  & =c-d \\\\  & =(2i+4j-3k)-(-i+5k) \\\\  & =3i+4j-8k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{DC}| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{89}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
